# The Capture

I finished watching [The Capture][], season 2 recently. (It's free to watch on
iView if you're in Australia).

[The Capture]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Capture_(TV_series)

Without spoiling too much, it's a fantastic UK conspiracy/cop/spy thriller
about weaponised deepfakes and their effect on society---particularly the
justice system.
The show covers their sinister use for political gain, and in corporate
and intelligence espionage.

It is not a true story, but it's becoming more and more true to life as AI
generated imagery, and is the focus of the show, _live camera feed
manipulation_ technology continues to [improve rapidly](https://www.youtube.com
/watch?v=wp-otuBK9HU).

It's a horrifying prediction of the world we are slowly inching towards day
by day. Where we can't trust anything that we see, video evidence is thrown out
of the courts completely and the intricacies of intelligence, espionage,
terrorism and politics are changed forever.

There is a third season---but I think season 2 wrapped it up quite nicely.
